# Optional. Supabase Auth and cloud preference sync.
# Only public, publishable client values belong here. VITE_* values are bundled
# into browser JavaScript and are visible to anyone who opens the app.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-public-anon-key

# What stays in the browser, in localStorage, and never in this file:
# - BYOK LLM API keys for Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter, and local Ollama endpoints.
# - Google and Notion calendar tokens.
# - Private Apple, Proton, and CalDAV calendar links.
# - Today's cached briefing, triage results, and quick events.

# What runs on Cloudflare Pages Functions, with no secret logged:
# - /api/rss fetches public RSS and Atom feeds. It validates URLs, blocks
#   private redirect targets, and caches successful feeds at the edge.
# - /api/ics fetches read-only calendar links over HTTPS. Responses are never
#   cached, and URLs or event details are never written to a log.

# Never put a service-role key, LLM key, Notion token, or private calendar URL
# in this file or in a VITE_* variable. If you add a server proxy later, keep
# its credentials in Cloudflare Pages environment secrets instead.
